(TestArcYZ_GimbalA.ngc - GimbalAB actuator-limits test)
(Quarter circle R=50mm in the YZ plane - G19 - while A gimbals 0 to 90deg)
(in sync with the arc so the tool stays aligned with the arc radius.)
(A rotates about X in GimbalAB kinematics, so the tilt is in the YZ plane.)

(CAUTION: PivotToChuckLength is 6in = 152.4mm. During this move the Y and Z)
(ACTUATORS travel to about -102mm while CAD coordinates stay within 0..50mm.)
(Verify actuator travel and soft limits, or run in Simulate first.)

(Nominal path: 78.54mm at F1200 = 20mm/s -> about 3.9 sec each way.)
(A must sweep 90deg over that time -> about 22.9 deg/sec demanded.)
(With Actuator Space Limits ON and actuator A Vel = 10 deg/sec the feed)
(should drop to about 44% -> about 9 sec each way. OFF -> full speed.)

G21 G90 G94
G43.4 H1 (TCP on)
G19            (arcs in the YZ plane)
G0 X0 Y0 Z0 A0 B0
G4 P0.5

G3 Y50 Z50 J0 K50 A90 F2000   (90deg arc up-and-over, A follows 0 to 90)
G4 P0.5
G2 Y0 Z0 J-50 K0 A0           (retrace back down, A returns to 0)

G17            (restore XY plane)
M2
